<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Главная's own measurements — the ones no other screen has a use for.

    A SEPARATE FILE AND NOT `dimens.xml`, for the same reason `strings_hub.xml` and
    `strings_flow.xml` exist: several waves work this tree at once, `dimens.xml` is
    the foundation's, and three agents appending to the bottom of one file is three
    conflicts in the same six lines. Android merges every `values/*.xml` into one
    table, so a name declared here is a name declared once.

    Nothing here starts a second ladder. Скругления, отступы, движение and the glyph
    sizes all live in `dimens.xml` / `motion.xml` and are referenced from there;
    what is below is either a WIDTH measured off one specific string, or an OPTICAL
    correction, and neither belongs on a shared scale.
-->
<resources>

    <!--
        «Добавить подписку» — the flyout's content width, sized to its longest
        option, «Добавить из буфера обмена», the same rule the `select_popup_w_*`
        set already follows. It carries a leading glyph and no check column:
        [ 10 ][ glyph 18 ][ 10 ][ label ][ 10 ].
    -->
    <dimen name="select_popup_w_add">216dp</dimen>

    <!--
        …and where it hangs. §6's 48 / 8 are measured off a full-width settings row
        inside a card; @id/btn_home_add is a 48dp icon with a 24dp glyph sitting
        4dp from the screen edge, so the same pair would open the flyout ON the
        button's bottom edge and leave its right edge 4dp short of the 16dp gutter
        every other block on Главная starts from.

        44 puts the top edge 8dp under the glyph's own bottom (12dp of padding +
        24dp of glyph = 36); 12 puts the right edge on the gutter (4dp of row
        padding + 12 = 16).
    -->
    <dimen name="select_popup_offset_top_add">44dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="select_popup_offset_right_add">12dp</dimen>

    <!--
        THE OPTICAL PULL FOR A GLYPH IN A 48dp TOUCH TARGET.

        A 22dp glyph centred in a 48dp box sits 13dp inside it, so a control laid
        out ON a gutter draws its glyph 13dp off that gutter and reads as indented
        from every line of text beside it. The sub-page toolbar solves the same
        problem from the other end (view_toolbar.xml: the back button is inset
        space_4 so its 24dp glyph lands ON the 16dp gutter); a control already
        sitting inside a padded card has no inset left to take, so it takes a pull.

        Negative on purpose, and it is NOT a spacing step: nothing may reach for it
        as a gap. One name, so the next control that needs it does not invent a
        second number.
    -->
    <dimen name="optical_nudge_touch_target">-10dp</dimen>

    <!--
        THE GAP AFTER THAT SAME BOX, and it is the other half of the pull above.

        The pull moves where the glyph is DRAWN; it does not make the box narrower. The
        chevron's 48dp box still ends 13dp past the right edge of its 22dp glyph, so a
        title laid out against the BOX begins 13dp further right than it looks — on top of
        whatever gap was asked for. With space_8 that made a 21dp trench between the glyph
        and the first letter of the подписка's name where the design asks for 16, and the
        owner read it as exactly that: «ник подписки … должно было сместится тоже левее
        вместе с этой кнопкой … чем много пустого пространства оставлять».

        16 (the design's gap after a leading element, view_row.xml) − 13 (the box's overhang
        past its glyph) = 3. So the OPTICAL gap is the design's 16 and the number here is
        what is left after the box's own overhang is paid for.

        Not a spacing step either, for the same reason as the pull: it is one arithmetic
        result, valid for a 22dp glyph in a 48dp box, and it moves only if the box or the
        glyph does.
    -->
    <dimen name="space_after_touch_target">3dp</dimen>

</resources>
